{"pageid": 953, "title": "Chimeratype", "revid": 2227, "categories": ["Chimeratypes", "Lore", "Monsters"], "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><figure class=\"thumb  show-info-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" style=\"width: 180px\"> \t<a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/d/d3/Chimeratype.png/revision/latest?cb=20241215001315\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"Chimeratype\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/d/d3/Chimeratype.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241215001315\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"180\" height=\"284\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-image-name=\"Chimeratype.png\" data-image-key=\"Chimeratype.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" /></a> \t \t<figcaption class=\"thumbcaption\"> \t\t \t\t\t<a href=\"/wiki/File:Chimeratype.png\" class=\"info-icon\"><svg><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-info-small\"></use></svg></a> \t\t \t\t \t\t \t</figcaption> </figure>\n<table align=\"center\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; border-style:none; background-color:transparent;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td width=\"20\" valign=\"top\" style=\"color:#7B68EE;font-size:40px;font-family:serif;font-weight:bold;text-align:left;padding:10px 10px;\">“\n</td>\n<td style=\"padding:4px 10px;\"><i>Simply put, they are the monsters from within. The man that becomes beast. When humankind's paranoia of each other manifests monsters in their place, most often in the shape of -- but not limited to -- animals.</i>\n</td>\n<td width=\"20\" valign=\"bottom\" style=\"color:#7B68EE;font-size:40px;font-family:serif;font-weight:bold;text-align:right;padding:10px 10px;\">”\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&#160;\n</td>\n<td valign=\"top\"><div style=\"line-height:1em;text-align: right\"><cite style=\"font-style:normal;\">&#8212; <i><a href=\"/wiki/Book_of_Butcher_1\" title=\"Book of Butcher 1\">The Book of Butcher</a></i></cite></div><i></i>\n</td></tr></tbody></table><p><b>Chimeratypes</b> are a breed of <a href=\"/wiki/Monsters\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Monsters\">monster</a> fought by <a href=\"/wiki/The_Order_of_St._George\" title=\"The Order of St. George\">The Order of St. George</a>. Coming from mankind's fear of becoming a beast, they are most commonly seen as werebeasts.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"History\">History</span></h2>\n<p>While the full history of this monster is unknown, they have appeared through multiple centuries and cultures across the planet. They were originally classified as <a href=\"/wiki/Mythotypes\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mythotypes\">Mythotypes</a> before their popularity shifted them into their own category.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-BOB&#95;1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-BOB-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Description\">Description</span></h2>\n<p>A mix between the <a href=\"/wiki/Animatype\" title=\"Animatype\">Animatype</a> and the <a href=\"/wiki/Duplicitype\" title=\"Duplicitype\">Duplicitype</a>, the Chimera originates from fears of a man becoming a monster, of giving into animalistic origins. With the most common type being a werebeast, this creature is believed to have originated in Europe as the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Werewolf\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Werewolf\">Werewolf</a>. Due to the common folklore surrounding this creature, they are usually very easy to kill, often with silver bullets or blades. However, assumptions can be the death of a hunter, and a thorough investigation should be put into what created the beast before the hunt begins.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Classifications\">Classifications</span></h3>\n<p>The most common Chimeratype is the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Werewolf\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Werewolf\">Werewolf</a>, usually in Western cultures. Other werebeasts can also be found, though, such as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kitsune\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Kitsune\">Kitsune</a>, Were-Leopards, Were-Bears, and Were-Rats.\n</p><p>A second classification of Chimeratype is the <b>Chimeratype Deviant.</b> They are able to transform into any animal, human, or, conceivably, monster. While they are rare, they are incredibly dangerous due to their methods of camouflage. Hunters are expected to bait them, trap them, and burn them to ash.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-BOB&#95;1-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-BOB-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notable_Animatypes\">Notable Animatypes</span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Animatype_Totems\">Animatype Totems</span></h3>\n<dl><dd><i>TBA</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Gallery\">Gallery</span></h2>\n<div id=\"gallery-0\" hash=\"0fbd8161c38d636aa1e8c87c1fe4fa2d\" data-seq-no=\"0\" class=\"wikia-gallery wikia-gallery-caption-below wikia-gallery-position-left wikia-gallery-spacing-medium wikia-gallery-border-small wikia-gallery-captions-left wikia-gallery-caption-size-medium\"><div class=\"wikia-gallery-caption\"></div><div class=\"wikia-gallery-item\" style=\"width:187px; \"><div class=\"thumb\" style=\"height:187px;\"><div class=\"gallery-image-wrapper accent\" id=\"Chimeratype-png\" style=\"position: relative; height:185px; width:117px;\"><a class=\"image lightbox\" href=\"/wiki/File:Chimeratype.png\" title=\"Chimeratype.png (2.18 MB)\" style=\"height:185px; width:117px;\"><noscript><img style=\"\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/d/d3/Chimeratype.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/117?cb=20241215001315\" title=\"Chimeratype.png (2.18 MB)\" class=\"thumbimage\" alt=\"\" height=\"185\" width=\"185\" data-image-name=\"Chimeratype.png\" data-image-key=\"Chimeratype.png\" data-relevant=\"1\"></noscript><img style=\"\" src=\"data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D\" title=\"Chimeratype.png (2.18 MB)\" class=\"thumbimage lazyload\" alt=\"\" height=\"185\" width=\"185\" data-image-name=\"Chimeratype.png\" data-image-key=\"Chimeratype.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" data-src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/d/d3/Chimeratype.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/117?cb=20241215001315\" /></a></div></div></div></div>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"References\">References</span></h2>\n<small><div style=\"width:auto; max-height:190px; overflow:auto; padding-left:0.5em; padding-right:0.5em; border-top-left-radius:0.5em; border-bottom-left-radius:0.5em\">\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-BOB-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-BOB_1-0\">1.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-BOB_1-1\">1.1</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/James_Tynion_IV\" title=\"James Tynion IV\">Tynion, James IV</a>. <i><a href=\"/wiki/Book_of_Butcher_1\" title=\"Book of Butcher 1\">Book of Butcher</a>,</i> vol. #1, <a href=\"/wiki/Book_of_Butcher_1\" title=\"Book of Butcher 1\">issue no.1</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Boom!_Studios\" title=\"Boom! Studios\">Boom! Studios</a>, 2023.</span>\n</li>\n</ol></div></div></small></div>", "fetched_at": "2026-10-28T22:43:33+00:00"}